- op: discuss  # 70d4
  at: '2026-02-18T14:01:12Z'  # 70d4
  by: agent  # 70d4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 70d4
  clock: 3  # 70d4
  nonce: 70d4  # 70d4
  message: "Kconfig analyzer: Linux kernel configuration files use a custom syntax with config, menuconfig, choice, depends on, select, and tristate keywords. No tree-sitter grammar exists; regex-based parsing of menu hierarchy and dependency graphs would work."  # 70d4
- op: discuss  # b777
  at: '2026-02-18T14:55:13Z'  # b777
  by: agent  # b777
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b777
  clock: 4  # b777
  nonce: b777  # b777
  message: "Kconfig tristate options (y/m/n) control whether code compiles as built-in, module, or excluded. The analyzer should model these as conditional compilation edges affecting which source files participate in the build."  # b777
